  "content": {
    "headline": "Love Island finalist reveals sad Casa Amor reality fans don't realise",
    "deck": "Love Island fans look forward to the Casa Amor twist every year, but it can be difficult for some Islanders",
    "byline": "Kimberly Nhundu",
    "date": "21 July 2026",
    "category": "TV",
    "topic": "Love Island",
    "hero_image": "https://i2-prod.ok.co.uk/article37459016.ece/ALTERNATES/s1200d/0_Love-Island-TV-Show-Series-13-Episode-44-Mallorca-Spain-14-Jul-2026.jpg",
    "hero_alt": "Julia Majchrzak on Love Island",
    "source_url": "https://www.ok.co.uk/tv/love-island-finalist-reveals-sad-37458508",
    "paragraphs": [
      "The new arrivals must find a solid connection to secure a spot in the main villa, which often means breaking up long-standing couples. Just weeks after this year's dramatic Casa Amor, finalist Julia Majchrzak is opening up about the twist fans rarely see.",
      "Fans at home instantly noticed that Julia was the only one trying to keep Martha in the villa out of solidarity, and it seems they were spot on.",
      "She explained that Casa girls often stick together because they know how hard it is to walk into an established villa and find safety in each other.",
      "Throughout their various tiffs in the house, the Casa girls stuck closely together. But Julia is the only one that has survived the evictions."
    ]
  },
